  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Capacity Building in Water Resource Management</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pakistan is a country with over 220 million population. The water resources of the country are under great pressure due to the increasing population, growing multi-sectoral needs, and the increasing impacts of climate change. It is crucial to understand the management of existing water resources from a holistic perspective for an equitable and sustainable future. IWRM is an effective approach to managing water, which requires a strong interface of science and policy. Though the National Water Policy 2018 and IWRM implantation guidelines are available but at the user end water water-related practices are very unsustainable. The project intends to develop the capacities of stakeholders in Pakistan for the implementation of the science-policy-practice interface.</narrative>
  </description>
